  "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/80be2cbe10b0d4ab72e273ef6761a4181d4af7b2e3cfefc11256b5280c2286e5.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $8$ units, so the distance equals $8.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/ba6df354884147449c1df49a494b2fe9bbb5313415509693eb58ac26ddfe5a15.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/564ad51f023caeb6aa9a9fc53f868a3a98710a2f42dd0417846278ac1a14a807.png)\n\nThe point $(-2,0)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(6,0)$ is at a distance of $6$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $6+2=8.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
